    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d802">

                <pb facs="0951" n="857" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg857"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr. Terrell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-07-10"><hi rendition="#italic">July 10,
                        1896.</hi></date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1018.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose for your information copy of a
                        letter<anchor n="1" xml:id="d802-f1"/> from R. D. Kimball concerning the
                    protection of his sister, Dr. Grace Kimball, and her associates at Van.</p>
                <p>Mr. Kimball has been assured that you fully appreciate the situation at Van, and
                    will afford all possible protection to American citizens residing there.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
